Description: Provides functions to download, clean, and standardize Brazilian
    public health microdata from DATASUS <https://datasus.saude.gov.br/>, the
    Department of Informatics of the Brazilian Unified Health System (SUS).
    Supported sources are the Mortality Information System (SIM), the Live
    Birth Information System (SINASC), the Hospital Information System (SIH),
    the Outpatient Information System (SIA), hospital beds from the National
    Registry of Health Establishments (CNES), oncology cases from the Oncology
    Panel (PO), and vaccination doses from the National Immunization Program
    Information System (SI-PNI). Data can be requested by state and year,
    compressed '.dbc' files are decompressed internally, and variable names and
    labels are available in English or Portuguese, so that the resulting data
    frames are ready for epidemiological and public health analyses.
